    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d19">

                <pb facs="0067" n="13" sameAs="frus:frus1944Quebec/pg13"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Prime Minister Churchill to President
                        Roosevelt</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d19-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1944-08-05">August 5, 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Prime Minister to President Roosevelt Personal and Top Secret number 744.</p>
                <p>Thank you so much for your 593.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d19-f2"/> Things are
                    everywhere approaching a climax, and almost always a climax in our favour.</p>
                <p>Please try to give me a firm date for <hi rendition="#small-caps">Octagon</hi> as
                    I have a lot to arrange.</p>
                <p>I am sure your journey to the Pacific must have strengthened the already buoyant
                    situation there. One of the most important things we have to settle when we meet
                    is what you want us to do in the Japanese finale and how we can do it, and also,
                    please, what we would like to do ourselves.</p>
                <p>Am off to Normandy tomorrow morning, returning evening, and on Wednesday
                        night<anchor n="3" xml:id="d19-f3"/> I leave for 10 days or a fortnight for
                        [<hi rendition="#italic">with?</hi>] Wilson, Devers, and Alexander.<anchor
                        n="4" xml:id="d19-f4"/> I shall be in full touch all the time and will
                    communicate as usual, which is saying a lot. Every good wish.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d19-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d19-f1-content">
                <p>Sent to Washington by the United States Military Attaché, London, via Army
                    channels; forwarded by the White House Map Room to Roosevelt, who was then in
                    Alaska, as telegram No. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Red</hi> 245.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d19-f2" n="2" xml:id="d19-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d19-f3" n="3" xml:id="d19-f3-content">
                <p>August 9, 1944; but Churchill’s departure was delayed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d19-f4" n="4" xml:id="d19-f4-content">
                <p>Concerning Churchill’s visit to Italy, August 11–28, 1944, see Churchill, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Triumph and Tragedy</hi>, pp. 86–127.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
